## PARKED — Disable old portal on .37:8080  (blocked on VPN)

The old Internal Marketing Portal is still live at `http://10.10.1.37:8080` (`/var/www/luci-hub`, built Jul 7), superseded by the current portal at `http://10.10.1.17:8081`. It's harmless but stale — disabling it is cleanup, not urgency.

**Blocker:** needs LAN/VPN access to `10.10.1.37` + an interactive sudo password (the agent's shell can provide neither).

**To do when back on VPN** — in Mac Terminal (or Cursor's integrated terminal), after pressing `Ctrl+C` to clear any stuck prompt, run:

```
bash ~/cleanup-luci-hub-37.sh
```

The script disables the `luci-hub` nginx site, reloads nginx, and archives `/var/www/luci-hub` → `/var/www/_archive/luci-hub-2026-07-16`. It verifies `:8080` goes 404/refused and `:80` (live site) stays 200. Reversible; undo commands are in the script header.

**After it's done:** run `curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" http://10.10.1.37:8080/` (expect 404/refused) and `curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" http://10.10.1.37/` (expect 200), then delete this section and commit.

